# Pairs with LogPrefixApplied, and reproduces issue #4621 as production had it:
# an append abandoned at its flush deadline (or by an expired drain) leaves the
# in-flight window, so the watermark no longer stops at it; a reader passes the
# offset, the abandoned provider call then lands, and the entry sits below the
# reader's position for ever. The base bounds the watermark by every unsettled
# abandoned append (WalAbandonedFlushRegistry).
MODULE: LogPrefixAppliedWatermarkIgnoresAbandoned
TARGET: LogPrefixApplied
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the watermark ignores an abandoned append, so it lands below a reader that passed it
PERTURBS: ReadStep

--- FIND
    /\ ReadFrom(l) < Watermark
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an abandoned append no longer bounds the reader's horizon.
    /\ ReadFrom(l) < Min({next, RecoveredNext} \cup inflight)
--- END